          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On January 19, 2009, at 6:46 PM, a witness was intrigued by a bright yellow clarity moving in the sky that separated into several distinct yellow/red lights. The phenomenon quickly faded away. The observation lasted between 10 and 15 seconds. The characteristics reported by the witness leave little doubt as to the nature of the phenomenon, consistent with the witness's second intuition, namely the observation of a bolide, likely due to the fall of a meteoroid or space debris. This case is classified as B, indicating a probable observation of a bolide (fall of a meteoroid or space debris).",
